      "summaries": {
        "en": "ESPectre is an open-source motion detection system that leverages Wi-Fi Channel State Information (CSI) from ESP32 microcontrollers to sense human movement without cameras or wearables. By analyzing subtle changes in Wi-Fi signal reflections caused by moving bodies, it achieves privacy-preserving presence detection. The system integrates seamlessly with Home Assistant, enabling smart home automation based on occupancy. You can deploy multiple ESP32 nodes to cover larger areas and tune sensitivity for different environments. Ideal for energy-saving, security, and elderly care applications.",
        "zh": "ESPectre 是基于Wi-Fi信道状态信息（CSI）的开源运动检测系统，利用ESP32微控制器分析人体移动对信号反射的细微变化，实现无摄像头、无穿戴设备的隐私保护式存在检测。其核心技术从物理层提取CSI数据，通过信号处理算法区分静态与动态环境，精准识别运动。系统原生集成Home Assistant，可触发智能家居自动化，部署多个ESP32节点可扩大覆盖范围，并支持灵敏度参数调整。适用于节能、安防、老人看护等隐私友好的占用检测场景。",
        "es": "ESPectre is an open-source motion detection system that leverages Wi-Fi Channel State Information (CSI) from ESP32 microcontrollers to sense human movement without cameras or wearables. By analyzing subtle changes in Wi-Fi signal reflections caused by moving bodies, it achieves privacy-preserving presence detection. The system integrates seamlessly with Home Assistant, enabling smart home automation based on occupancy. You can deploy multiple ESP32 nodes to cover larger areas and tune sensitivity for different environments. Ideal for energy-saving, security, and elderly care applications.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "espectre stands out for csi, diy, and esp-32 in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "ESPectre is an open-source motion detection system that leverages Wi-Fi Channel State Information (CSI) from ESP32 microcontrollers to sense human movement without cameras or wearables. By analyzing subtle changes in Wi-Fi signal reflections caused by moving bodies, it achieves privacy-preserving presence detection. The system integrates seamlessly with Home Assistant, enabling smart home automation based on occupancy. You can deploy multiple ESP32 nodes to cover larger areas and tune sensitivity for different environments. Ideal for energy-saving, security, and elderly care applications.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/francescopace/espectre for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
