      "summaries": {
        "en": "OpenMed is an open-source healthcare AI toolkit that enables on-device and on-premise deployment of LLMs for medical tasks. It leverages models like BERT, DeepSeek, and Qwen for tasks such as named entity recognition (NER) and PII detection, optimized for iOS via MLX. Its key strength is privacy-preserving, offline inference, making it ideal for clinical settings where data security is critical. Developers can integrate OpenMed into healthcare apps to analyze medical records locally, reducing reliance on cloud services.",
        "zh": "OpenMed是一个开源医疗AI工具包，专注于设备端和本地部署大语言模型，以解决医疗场景的隐私与实时性问题。它整合BERT、DeepSeek、Qwen等模型，支持命名实体识别（NER）和PII检测等任务，并通过MLX框架针对iOS设备优化。其核心优势在于离线推理，确保患者数据不出设备，符合医疗数据安全要求。开发者可将OpenMed嵌入应用，本地分析电子病历或检测敏感信息，无需依赖云端，适用于诊所、医院等低延迟和高隐私保护场景。",
        "es": "OpenMed is an open-source healthcare AI toolkit that enables on-device and on-premise deployment of LLMs for medical tasks. It leverages models like BERT, DeepSeek, and Qwen for tasks such as named entity recognition (NER) and PII detection, optimized for iOS via MLX. Its key strength is privacy-preserving, offline inference, making it ideal for clinical settings where data security is critical. Developers can integrate OpenMed into healthcare apps to analyze medical records locally, reducing reliance on cloud services.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "openmed stands out for bert, deepseek, and healthcare in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "OpenMed is an open-source healthcare AI toolkit that enables on-device and on-premise deployment of LLMs for medical tasks. It leverages models like BERT, DeepSeek, and Qwen for tasks such as named entity recognition (NER) and PII detection, optimized for iOS via MLX. Its key strength is privacy-preserving, offline inference, making it ideal for clinical settings where data security is critical. Developers can integrate OpenMed into healthcare apps to analyze medical records locally, reducing reliance on cloud services.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/maziyarpanahi/openmed for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
