      "summaries": {
        "en": "React is a JavaScript library for building user interfaces, solving the challenge of efficiently updating and rendering UI components as data changes. Its key innovation is the virtual DOM, which minimizes direct DOM manipulation by computing differences and applying minimal updates. Developers can use React to create interactive web apps with reusable components, manage state with hooks or external libraries, and extend it with frameworks like Next.js for server-side rendering or React Native for mobile apps.",
        "zh": "React 是一个用于构建用户界面的 JavaScript 库，核心目标是解决数据变化时高效更新和渲染 UI 组件的难题。其关键技术是虚拟 DOM，通过计算差异并执行最小化更新，避免直接操作真实 DOM 的性能开销。开发者可以用 React 创建可复用的组件，利用 Hooks 管理状态，或结合 Redux 等库处理复杂数据流。实际应用中，React 可搭配 Next.js 实现服务端渲染以提升 SEO，或通过 React Native 开发跨平台移动应用。它的声明式编程风格让 UI 逻辑更清晰，组件化架构便于维护和扩展，是构建现代 Web 应用的基础工具。",
        "es": "React is a JavaScript library for building user interfaces, solving the challenge of efficiently updating and rendering UI components as data changes. Its key innovation is the virtual DOM, which minimizes direct DOM manipulation by computing differences and applying minimal updates. Developers can use React to create interactive web apps with reusable components, manage state with hooks or external libraries, and extend it with frameworks like Next.js for server-side rendering or React Native for mobile apps.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "react stands out for declarative, frontend, and javascript in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "React is a JavaScript library for building user interfaces, solving the challenge of efficiently updating and rendering UI components as data changes. Its key innovation is the virtual DOM, which minimizes direct DOM manipulation by computing differences and applying minimal updates. Developers can use React to create interactive web apps with reusable components, manage state with hooks or external libraries, and extend it with frameworks like Next.js for server-side rendering or React Native for mobile apps.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/react/react for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
