      "summaries": {
        "en": "React Native is a framework for building native mobile apps using React. It bridges JavaScript and native platform code, enabling developers to write UI components in React that render as native widgets. Its key strength is code reuse across iOS and Android while maintaining near-native performance. You can start by creating a new project with `npx react-native init`, then build and deploy to both platforms from a single codebase.",
        "zh": "React Native 是一个用 React 构建原生移动应用的框架。它通过桥接 JavaScript 与原生平台代码，让开发者用 React 编写 UI 组件，这些组件最终渲染为原生控件。其核心优势在于跨平台代码复用（iOS 和 Android），同时保持接近原生的性能。你可以通过 `npx react-native init` 创建新项目，从单一代码库构建并部署到两个平台。",
        "es": "React Native is a framework for building native mobile apps using React. It bridges JavaScript and native platform code, enabling developers to write UI components in React that render as native widgets. Its key strength is code reuse across iOS and Android while maintaining near-native performance. You can start by creating a new project with `npx react-native init`, then build and deploy to both platforms from a single codebase.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "react-native stands out for android, app-framework, and cross-platform in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "React Native is a framework for building native mobile apps using React. It bridges JavaScript and native platform code, enabling developers to write UI components in React that render as native widgets. Its key strength is code reuse across iOS and Android while maintaining near-native performance. You can start by creating a new project with `npx react-native init`, then build and deploy to both platforms from a single codebase.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/react/react-native for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
